WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.296 --> 00:00:01.629
(bright violin music)

00:00:01.629 --> 00:00:03.400
- [Narrator] Once a hub of
French aristocratic parties,

00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:05.459
this castle in the
countryside lies abandoned

00:00:05.459 --> 00:00:08.542
after falling victim to a house fire.

00:00:14.179 --> 00:00:16.006
A few hours outside Paris are the remains

00:00:16.006 --> 00:00:19.817
of the chateau de La Mothe-Chandeniers.

00:00:19.817 --> 00:00:21.549
The castle was built in the 14th century

00:00:21.549 --> 00:00:24.257
and was owned by French nobles.

00:00:24.257 --> 00:00:26.567
It was conquered twice by the
British in the Middle Ages

00:00:26.567 --> 00:00:29.954
and was devastated during
the French Revolution.

00:00:29.954 --> 00:00:32.028
Around 60 years later,
after a wealthy relative

00:00:32.028 --> 00:00:34.628
of Napoleon III took control,
he restored the castle

00:00:34.628 --> 00:00:36.295
to its former glory.

00:00:37.436 --> 00:00:41.047
However, in 1932, just after
central heating was installed,

00:00:41.047 --> 00:00:43.130
a violent fire broke out.

00:00:44.727 --> 00:00:47.116
Since the fire, the castle
has been slowly taken over

00:00:47.116 --> 00:00:48.233
by nature.

00:00:48.233 --> 00:00:49.713
Trees have grown through the interior,

00:00:49.713 --> 00:00:53.553
and vines crawl along the
once sturdy castle walls.

00:00:53.553 --> 00:00:55.076
Though its fate is still uncertain,

00:00:55.076 --> 00:00:56.953
today there are efforts to save the castle

00:00:56.953 --> 00:01:00.953
with a group raising money
to restore the ruins.

